// Question bank in simple English.
//
// Each entry is [question, whatTheyAreChecking, whatToSay]. The third item is
// written to be spoken out loud, in short sentences, with no words the reader
// would have to look up.

export const bankIntro = `An interviewer rarely stops at your first answer. They ask something open, they listen, and then they push on the weakest part of what you said. That second question is where most people fail. Not because they do not know the system, but because they only practised the first answer.\n\nSo the questions below are in three groups. **Opening** questions are the ones you will be asked first. **Follow-up** questions come after your answer, and these are the ones to practise out loud. **Extension** questions ask what you would do if things changed. They are not testing memory. They are testing whether you can think.\n\nEach question has two parts under it. **They are checking** tells you what the interviewer actually wants to find out. **Say this** is a full answer you can speak. Do not memorise it word for word. Read it, understand why it is built that way, then say it in your own words.`;

